ca-06017-bos-matter-40588.title:
Treasurer-Tax Collector's Office recommending the Board approve the following:
1) Make findings that it is appropriate to engage an independent contractor to provide Countywide banking services, as Agreement 10532 can be more economically and feasibly performed by independent contractors than County employees in accordance with County ordinance code 3.13.030(A);
2) Award Bid 2026-0100 for the purchase of banking services to the lowest responsive bidder, Bank of America;
3) Approve and authorize the Chair to sign, competitively procured, Agreement 10532 with Bank of America, for the provision of banking services, effective upon execution for a period of 3 years, with 2 one-year options to extend, for a total possible term of 5 years in the amount of $250,000; and
4) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to execute amendments relating to Agreement10532, contingent upon approval by County Counsel and Risk Management, which do not increase the maximum dollar amount or term of the Agreement. 

FUNDING: General Fund.

ca-06017-bos-matter-41365.title:
Probation Department recommending the Board:
1) Make findings in accordance with El Dorado County Ordinance Code Section 3.13.030(B) that adult and juvenile sex offender counseling services requires specialty skills and qualifications not expressly identified in County classifications; 
2) Make findings in accordance with Procurement Policy C-17 Section 3.6.G.6 that Agreement 10412 is exempt from competitive bidding because the continuity of providers will provide efficiency or critical knowledge, and other providers cannot provide;
3) Approve and authorize the Chair to sign Agreement 10412 with Fostering Connections, in the amount of $175,000, to commence upon execution, and end three years thereafter; and
4) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to execute amendments relating to Agreement 10412, contingent upon approval by County Counsel and Risk Management, which do not increase the maximum dollar amount or term of the Agreement.
 
FUNDING:  AB109 (Public Safety Realignment) (85%), Juvenile Justice Realignment Block Grant (SB 823) (15%).

ca-06017-bos-matter-41377.title:
Department of Transportation recommending the Board adopt and authorize the Chair to sign Resolution 178-2026, rescinding prior Resolution 164-2018 which established imprest accounts for the Department of Transportation in the total amount of $11,400, and reestablishing imprest cash funds in the cumulative amount of $21,400, consisting of: 
1) $21,000 for Emergency Road/Snow Operations; 
2) $200 for Department of Transportation's Development, Right-of-Way, and Environmental Unit; 
3) $100 for the Placerville Department of Transportation's Office; and 
4) $100 for the South Lake Tahoe Department of Transportation's Office.
 
FUNDING:  Road Fund.  (100% - Local)

ca-06017-bos-matter-41441.title:
Department of Transportation, Maintenance and Operations Division, Fleet Services Unit, recommending the Board:
1) Find the purchase of eleven (11) replacement vehicles are exempt from competitive bidding in accordance with Procurement Policy C-17, Section 3.4.4, due to use of State of California competitively-bid Contracts 1-22-23-23 and 1-22-23-20;  
2) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to utilize the State of California Contract 1-22-23-23 for the acquisition of nine (9) fleet replacement mid-size SUVs, and State of California Contract 1-22-23-20 for the acquisition of one (1) fleet replacement 1/2 ton truck and one (1) fleet replacement 3/4 ton truck for the Department of Transportation - Fleet Services Unit;
3) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to sign a purchase order to the awarded State vendor, Elk Grove Auto of Elk Grove, CA. in the amount of $377,238 plus applicable delivery, fees and taxes (estimated at $29,598.99) for a one time purchase of nine (9) replacement vehicles following Board approval; and 
4) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to sign a purchase order to the awarded State vendor,Winner Chevrolet of Colfax, CA. in the amount of $126,492 pus applicable delivery, fees and taxes (estimated at $9,670.50) for a one time purchase of two (2) fleet replacement trucks following Board approval.
 
FUNDING:  Fleet Internal Service Fund (100%).

ca-06017-bos-matter-41479.title:
Chief Administrative Office recommending the Board:
1) Find that a public benefit is derived from supporting a regional shared services model on the Georgetown Divide;
2) Approve and authorize the Chair to sign a Funding Agreement with Garden Valley Fire Protection District in the total amount of $400,000, for a term effective upon final execution for a two-year period, in support of a regional shared services model on the Georgetown Divide;
3) Authorize the Chief Administrative Officer to execute amendments relating to the Agreement, contingent upon approval by County Counsel and Risk Management, which do not increase the maximum dollar amount or term of the Agreement; and
4) Disband the Jurisdictional Reorganization Ad Hoc Committee.
 
FUNDING: Mosquito Fire Settlement Funds. (General Fund)

ca-06017-bos-matter-41501.title:
Sheriff’s Office recommending the Board:
1) Make findings in accordance with Ordinance 3.13.030(b) that law enforcement vehicle tear down and build up services are in the best interest of the public and that there are specialty skills, qualifications, and equipment not expressly identified in County classifications involved in the performance of the work;
2) Make findings in accordance with Procurement Policy C-17 Section 3.6 (E), exempting the competitive bidding process for Agreement 10666 because the procurement is utilizing a competitively bid contract with another public agency;
3) Approve and authorize the Chair to sign Agreement 10666, with Lehr Upfitters Opco LLC (doing business as LEHR), utilizing Placer County's contract, to provide law enforcement vehicle tear down and build up services with a retroactive term of October 1, 2026, to January 31, 2027, in the amount of $250,000;
4) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to execute amendments relating to Agreement 10666 that do not increase the total compensation amount of the Agreement, contingent upon approval by County Counsel and Risk Management; and
5) Authorize the Purchasing Agent to extend the agreement if Placer County elects to extend the original agreement, contingent on approval from County Counsel and Risk Management. 
 
FUNDING:  General Fund.
